    "fantasyOutlook": [
      "Johnson is a handcuff with real contingency value, not a player to treat as an immediate weekly starter. A reasonable 2026 expectation is roughly 70-110 touches if Walker stays healthy, with a path to more if Johnson wins the passing-down trust that Demercado currently owns. The rookie-draft price is fair around pick 28 in superflex formats, especially in .5 PPR where his receiving ability gives him a floor beyond pure early-down work. KTC’s 2,537 superflex value and Tier 8 label reflect the uncertainty, while FantasyPros’ consensus rookie rank of 17 is a useful reminder that the talent profile outruns the depth-chart rank.",
      "Dynasty managers should buy the player only at the right discount. Walker’s contract and Kansas City’s committee options suppress 2026 volume, but Johnson’s age, four-year production and receiving résumé create a credible 2027 breakout window. He is a strong late-first/early-second rookie selection in superflex leagues, with more appeal to contenders who can wait than to teams needing immediate lineup points."
    ],
    "comp": "A more compact, less explosive version of James White, with Nebraska’s volume showing he can handle far more early-down work.",
    "bottomLine": "Draft Johnson as a premium handcuff and patient dynasty stash, not as Kansas City’s Week 1 starter. His route to value is clear: pass protection, receiving detail and one Walker injury could turn a Day 3 pick into a league-winning contingency back.",
